WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:03.167
Roscoe wiped sweat from his brow.

2
00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:05.217
"Let's get some juice, Deputy.

3
00:00:05.218 --> 00:00:09.376
Then we'll discuss real suspects."

4
00:00:09.377 --> 00:00:12.474
They went to the saloon.

5
00:00:12.475 --> 00:00:15.205
Cleo swung the doors open.

6
00:00:15.206 --> 00:00:18.070
"The ice workers!"

7
00:00:18.071 --> 00:00:20.183
"Right!" Roscoe said.

8
00:00:20.184 --> 00:00:22.133
"Emmett and Bucky wanted that gold!

9
00:00:22.134 --> 00:00:23.809
We should . . . Cleo?"

10
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:26.541
His deputy wasn't moving.

11
00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:30.019
He stepped closer and gasped.

12
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.919
Emmett and Bucky were in the saloon with their slingshots drawn.

13
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.280
The whole place was silent.

14
00:00:37.281 --> 00:00:40.079
Folks looked mighty scared!

15
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:46.491
"Drop your slingshots and come in!" Emmett said.

16
00:00:46.492 --> 00:00:49.611
Roscoe nodded to Cleo.

17
00:00:49.612 --> 00:00:55.570
They put down their slingshots and entered.

18
00:00:55.571 --> 00:01:00.600
"You stole Jake's horses and cut the telegraph wire," Roscoe said.

19
00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:03.639
"We put the horses back," Bucky said.

20
00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:06.197
"Now give us our gold!"

21
00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:09.145
"It's locked up," Roscoe said.

22
00:01:09.146 --> 00:01:11.780
"You'll never get it."

23
00:01:11.781 --> 00:01:14.832
Fwap! Emmett shot a pebble.

24
00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:18.259
It shattered a glass.

25
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.011
Roscoe ducked as another pebble flew.

26
00:01:23.012 --> 00:01:27.253
Then he heard Emmett yelp.

27
00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:32.130
Roscoe peeked out. Fwap! Fwap!

28
00:01:32.131 --> 00:01:37.298
Federal marshals stood in the doorway, firing at the workers.

29
00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:43.694
"Cleo!" Roscoe waved.

30
00:01:43.695 --> 00:01:46.824
They rushed outside for their slingshots.

31
00:01:46.825 --> 00:01:51.187
Meanwhile Emmett and Bucky escaped through a back door.

32
00:01:51.188 --> 00:01:54.201
"Stop right there!" the marshals shouted.

33
00:01:54.202 --> 00:01:58.040
They ran after the ice workers, and so did Roscoe.

34
00:01:58.041 --> 00:02:02.499
But Cleo stayed outside, staring up at the roof.

35
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:08.389
That sneaky cat had a sneaky idea!

36
00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:14.279
She climbed onto the roof and raced to the back. Below,

37
00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.608
Emmett and Bucky were surrounded, but they weren't giving up. Fwap!

38
00:02:19.652 --> 00:02:25.747
Fwap! Cleo knocked those slingshots right out of their paws! "Yikes!"

39
00:02:25.748 --> 00:02:28.567
Emmett cried. Bucky

40
00:02:28.568 --> 00:02:35.659
held up his paws. "We surrender!" ***

41
00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.938
Everyone was in the sheriff's office.

42
00:02:38.939 --> 00:02:43.817
"The news about the lost gold spread fast," one marshal said.

43
00:02:43.818 --> 00:02:47.189
"We were looking for it in other towns."

44
00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:52.030
"How did the sack get into that ice?" Cleo asked.

45
00:02:52.031 --> 00:02:56.048
"Thieves threw it in a lake last fall," the marshal said.

46
00:02:56.049 --> 00:03:00.330
"They planned to come back for it, but we caught them."

47
00:03:00.331 --> 00:03:02.666
The other marshal nodded.

48
00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:07.675
"The lake froze in winter, and the ice company harvested the ice.

49
00:03:07.676 --> 00:03:11.610
The ice was stored until spring."

50
00:03:11.611 --> 00:03:17.229
Roscoe chuckled. "Finally the gold came here."

51
00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.761
He went to the safe.

52
00:03:19.762 --> 00:03:25.317
"Let's see. The combination is . . . 38 maybe?

53
00:03:25.318 --> 00:03:30.588
No, there was a five . . . Or was it a six?" He gulped.

54
00:03:30.589 --> 00:03:33.763
"I can't remember the combination!"

55
00:03:33.771 --> 00:03:39.511
Cleo grinned. "Step aside, Sheriff."

56
00:03:39.512 --> 00:03:41.801
The cat put her ear to the safe.

57
00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:45.874
Slowly she turned the dial.

58
00:03:45.875 --> 00:03:50.584
After a few minutes, the safe popped open!

59
00:03:50.585 --> 00:03:55.765
"You know how to open safes?" Roscoe shook his head.

60
00:03:55.766 --> 00:04:06.945
"I changed my mind, Deputy. You have lots of useful skills!"

